# The contamination gate's hashed denylist.
#
# One SHA-256 per line, of a lowercased term with its words joined by single
# spaces. Comments and blank lines are ignored. The clear text of a real term
# never appears in this file, in this repository, or in any repository: that
# is the whole point, and it is what lets this list run in public continuous
# integration.
#
# How a hash is made: lowercase the term, replace every character that is not
# a letter or a digit with a space, collapse the spaces, then sha256 the
# result. scripts/gate/README.md has the one-liner.
#
# Minimum term length is six characters with spaces removed to limit noisy
# matches. Hashes avoid literal disclosure but are vulnerable to guessing;
# they are not secret storage. Short terms need the separate literal sweep.
#
# The four hashes below are the canary. The canary is an invented business
# name that exists nowhere but this repository. It is never a real client, a
# real person or a real company. It is here so the gate can prove it still
# works.
#
# One of them is deliberately four words long. The first version of the
# matcher capped phrases at three words, so a four word entry could never
# match and the list would have lied about what it covered. The self-test now
# proves the four word case, and tests/gate/gate-cases.sh proves it again
# against a throwaway repository.

